  2048     118.7,118.1 -> 278.5,277.8         2.35    17301 -> 7363 ms     31.64 -> 31.51        5611 -> 5604           871
  Sampled GPU power (mean) base 36.1-39.6 W, new 33.8-39.0 W (the same 40 W cap; the new run is also shorter). No efficiency claim.
  Per stage at 512 tokens (bench --profile, one pass): MLP 2019 -> 511 ms (3.9x, 1.15 -> 4.54 TFLOP/s), QKV projections 943 -> 251 ms (3.8x,
  0.55 -> 2.05), attention output 287 -> 77 ms (3.7x, 1.20 -> 4.46), whole pass 4008 -> 1668 ms. DeltaNet recurrence 694 -> 763 ms
  (unchanged; it is now 46% of prefill), attention 43 -> 42 ms.
  Matched tasks through marin serve (ctx 4096, greedy, 64 tokens, 3 runs x 2 builds, text identical base/new and across runs):
    code review of 6,000 characters of Rust (about 1.4k tokens): first token 10.2 s -> 5.0 s (-51%), whole answer 12.2 -> 7.0 s
    chat question (about 30 tokens):                             first token 0.21-0.27 s -> 0.17-0.20 s (-20%; fixed costs dominate a short prompt)
  Numerics: pinned 128-step HF check, Qwen3.5-4B Q8 CUDA: PASS, token choices match, max logit diff 1.19e-5 (was 1.31e-5), max layer diff
  1.15e-5 (1.18e-5), normalized max 4.442e-6 (3.879e-6), relative RMS 3.027e-6 (3.288e-6); short reference PASS (1.53e-5 / 5.3e-6 / 1.7e-6).
  New regression test precise_int8_matmul_is_float32_grade_on_the_tensor_core_path (fails with the 2-part split, passes with the 3-part one).

=== DECISION ===
GO. All kernel and end-to-end gates met except the chat sub-gate of P2 (short chat -20% against 30%: a 30-token prompt is mostly fixed cost,
not projection time; prefill-heavy code prompts gain 51%). Remaining prefill bottleneck: the DeltaNet recurrence (46% at 512 tokens).
